  "prefLabel": "Env-A 605.02 Proof of Right, Title, and Interest; Good Standing",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 605.02 Proof of Right, Title, and Interest; Good Standing.\n\n(a) The department shall consider an application only when the applicant has certified that the applicant, or the owner or operator the applicant represents, has right, title, or interest in all of the property that is proposed for development or use because the owner or operator owns, leases, or has binding options to purchase all of the property proposed for development or use.\n\n(b) The owner or operator shall bear the burden of proving right, title, and interest in the property.\n\n(c) An owner or operator that is an entity which is required by RSA 292, RSA 293, RSA 293-A, or other applicable provision of New Hampshire law to register with the New Hampshire secretary of state shall show proof of being registered and in good standing to do business in New Hampshire.\n\nSource. #1710, eff 1-19-81; ss by #2332, eff 4-29-83; ss by #2938, eff 12-27-84; ss by #5033, eff 12-27-90; ss by #6057-B, eff 6-30-95; ss by #7879, eff 4-26-03; ss by #8129, eff 7-28-04; ss by #10000, eff 10-1-11; ss by #10175, eff 9-1-12; ss by #13510, eff 12-17-22",
